"""Long-form article: Best LED Light Bars & Light Kits for 2019–2026 Ram 1500 (5th gen, DT).
Mirrors the approved pilot (ford_f150_2021_tonneau.py) and the Silverado / F-150 / Tundra light-bar pages. No invented
hands-on testing: every spec comes from the maker/retailer pages listed in sources (checked 2026-10-05) or is quoted
from the Amazon listing title and marked as such. Bars are mostly universal; what is Ram-specific is the mount
(factory grille slots, hidden bumper, Rebel/TRX fog pockets, hood / A-pillar ditch mounts, roof), the Classic (DS)
sold alongside through 2024, and the 2025 front-end change. Stellantis' 2025 release is the source for the new
grille and headlamps; Baja Designs' Rebel/TRX hub (every kit 2019-24 or 2021-24), Rough Country titles (19-24) and
Diode Dynamics titles (2019-2024) are the source for where fit lists stop. Rough Country's own site was not opened;
its two documented kits are described from Battle Born Offroad (70783) and Tasca Parts (70781). The ZROADZ roof kit
is described from Lift Kits 4 Less (Z334721-KIT-C); the Amazon title prints Z334571-KIT-C, and the text tells readers
to confirm the part number. Diode Dynamics, Rigid and the budget bracket listings are title-only. Auxiliary switches:
Stellantis mentions an accessory switch bank (2025) and an RHO-only multifunction switch bank, but not spare
circuits for add-on lights, so the page says we could not confirm. DT six-lug wheels are from Wikipedia; the
Classic's five-lug wheels match the site's Ram pillar and bed-rack guide.
"""

